   "source": [
    "## 4. Part B - ANN architecture and development experiments\n",
    "\n",
    "The prescribed 64/32/16 ReLU layers learn nonlinear combinations of operating parameters.\n",
    "The two dropout layers randomly suppress 20% of activations during training, providing\n",
    "regularisation; dropout is disabled for validation and inference. A two-unit Softmax maps\n",
    "outputs to class probabilities, with sparse categorical crossentropy for integer labels.\n",
    "Adam starts at 0.001. The network has 3,410 trainable parameters.\n",
    "\n",
    "ReLU avoids saturation for positive inputs, but fixed widths do not establish an optimal\n",
    "architecture. Batch size changes update frequency and noise, while early stopping and\n",
    "LR reduction use validation loss. Both sklearn MLP and Keras ANN are neural networks;\n",
    "the brief groups them by implementation library. Differences include dropout, batch size,\n",
    "objective details and stopping behaviour, not fundamentally unrelated model families.\n",
    "\n",
    "All trials use identical fit/validation rows, a fit-only scaler and fresh seeded models.\n",
    "A 10-epoch batch-32 pilot precedes three fresh trials capped at 50 epochs. Callback\n",
    "`min_delta=0` is explicit; LR is halved after five non-improving epochs, down to 1e-6.\n",
    "The batch-16 trial remains a development result, outside the four core final configurations."
   ]
  },
